{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-49895" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{6}{\\sqrt[7]{x}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067951/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ae52e7a07df296b61c2fdb4097fe3c07b607c9cb28b3db06216439cdc10e33"} {"question" "q-49895" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This is an improper integral of the second kind because the function under the integral is unbounded at the *lower* limit of integration. \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{6}{\\sqrt[7]{x}}\\to \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to {0}^{+}\n$$\n\nNonetheless, it is possible to calculate the integral by setting the *lower* bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to {0}^{+}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[7]{x}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to {0}^{+}}{\\int }_{a}^{1}\\frac{6}{\\sqrt[7]{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to {0}^{+}}{\\int }_{a}^{1}6{x}^{-1/7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to {0}^{+}}7{x}^{6/7}{|}_{a}^{1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to {0}^{+}}7\\sqrt[7]{{x}^{6}}{|}_{a}^{1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to {0}^{+}}[7\\cdot \\sqrt[7]{{1}^{6}}-7\\cdot \\sqrt[7]{{a}^{6}}] \\\\  & =7(1)-7(0) \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067951/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ae52e7a07df296b61c2fdb4097fe3c07b607c9cb28b3db06216439cdc10e33"} {"question" "q-49895" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067951/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9ea38ea54540e2604c350ac4bfd17b8d0f73d36a19c93ad772f2e6ecf27dc465"} {"question" "q-49895" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/h