-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({\\int }_{a}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x(x+1)}\\,)"] ["math" "{lim}_{a\\to -{2}^{+}}({\\int }_{a}^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x(x+1)}\\,)"] ["math" "{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({\\int }_{0}^{a}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x(x+1)}\\,)"] ["math" "{lim}_{a\\to {0}^{+}}({\\int }_{a}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x(x+1)}\\,)"] ["math" "{lim}_{a\\to {2}^{-}}({\\int }_{0}^{a}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x(x+1)}\\,)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067951/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ae52e7a07df296b61c2fdb4097fe3c07b607c9cb28b3db06216439cdc10e33"} {"question" "q-141132" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{a\\to {0}^{+}}({\\int }_{a}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x(x+1)}\\,)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067951/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ae52e7a07df296b61c2fdb4097fe3c07b607c9cb28b3db06216439cdc10e33"} {"question" "q-141181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to \n${\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{4-{x}^{2}}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067951/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ae52e7a07df296b61c2fdb4097fe3c07b607c9cb28b3db06216439cdc10e33"} {"question" "q-141181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This is an improper integral of the second kind because the function under the integral is unbounded as we approach the *upper* integration limit from any point that lies in the interval $x\\in (-1,2):$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{4-{x}^{2}}\\to \\infty \\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to {2}^{-}\n$$\n\nWe can attempt to evaluate this integral by integrating $f(x)$ over the interval $x\\in [-1,b]$ and taking the limit as $b\\to {2}^{-}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{4-{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{b\\to {2}^{-}}({\\int }_{-1}^{b}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{4-{x}^{2}})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067951/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ae52e7a07df296b61c2fdb4097fe3c07b607c9cb28b3db06216439cdc10e33"} {"question" "q-141181" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067951/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9ea38ea54540e2604c350ac4bfd17b8d0f73d36a19c93ad772f2e6ecf27dc465"} {"question" "q-141181" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067951/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ae52e7a07df296b61c2fdb4097fe3c07b607c9cb28b3db06216439cdc10e33"} {"question" "q-141181" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{lim}_{b\\to (-1)^{+}}({\\int }_{b}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{4-{x}^{2}})"] ["math" "{lim}_{b\\to -\\infty }({\\int }_{b}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{4-{x}^{2}})"] ["math" "{lim}_{b\\to \\infty }({\\int }_{-1}^{b}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{4-{x}^{2}})"] ["math" "{lim}_{b\\to {0}^{-}}({\\int }_{-1}^{b}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{4-{x}^{2}})"] ["math" "{lim}_{b\\to {2}^{-}}({\\int }_{-1}^{b}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{4-{x}^{2}})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067951/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ae52e7a07df296b61c2fdb4097fe3c07b607c9cb28b3db06216439cdc10e33"} {"question" "q-141181" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{lim}_{b\\to {2}^{-}}({\\int }_{-1}^{b}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{4-{x}^{2}})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067951/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ae52e7a07df296b61c2fdb4097fe3c07b607c9cb28b3db06216439cdc10e33"} {"question" "q-347669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{2/3}^{22}\\frac{1}{(3x-2)^{1/3}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067951/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ae52e7a07df296b61c2fdb4097fe3c07b607c9cb28b3db06216439cdc10e33"} {"question" "q-347669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's rewrite the integral using a substitution. Let $u=3x-2.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe use the table below to change the limits:\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $22$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $64$ |\n\nCarrying out the change of variable, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2/3}^{22}\\frac{1}{(3x-2)^{1/3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{64}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{3{u}^{1/3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{64}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{{u}^{1/3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is an improper integral of the second kind because the function under the integral is unbounded at the *lower* limit of integration.\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\frac{1}{{u}^{1/3}}\\to \\infty \\,\\text{ as }\\,u\\to {0}^{+}.\n$$\n\nNonetheless, it is possible to calculate the integral by setting the *lower* bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to {0}^{+}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{64}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{{u}^{1/3}} & ={lim}_{a\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{a}^{64}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{{u}^{1/3}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{a}^{64}{u}^{-1/3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {\\frac{3}{2}\\,{u}^{2/3}|}_{a}^{64} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{1}{2}{\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}}|}_{a}^{64} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to {0}^{+}}[\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt[3]{{64}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt[3]{{a}^{2}}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16-0 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2/3}^{22}\\frac{1}{(3x-2)^{1/3}}\\,\\text{d}x=8.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067951/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ae52e7a07df296b61c2fdb4097fe3c07b607c9cb28b3db06216439cdc10e33"} {"question" "q-347669" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067951/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9ea38ea54540e2604c350ac4bfd17b8d0f73d36a19c93ad772f2e6ecf27dc465"} {"question" "q-347669" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067951/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ae52e7a07df296b61c2fdb4097fe3c07b607c9cb28b3db06216439cdc10e33"} {"question" "q-347669" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067951/state.json" "file_sha256" "84ae52e7a07df296b61c2fdb4097fe3c07b607c9cb28b3db06216439cdc10e33"}] "usage" {"q-82704" []} "basis" 2266 "retractions" [[17592186083852 :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to\n\n$\\displaystyle \\int_{-6}^{-3}\\frac{dx}{\\sqrt{x^{2} - 9}}$?"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186082479 17592186082480 17592186082481 17592186082482 17592186082483] "immutable_fields" [[17592186082478 :answer-field/correct] [17592186082478 :answer-field/id] [17592186082478 :answer-field/key] [17592186082478 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
